<title>UK: B.A.T lifted by Maryland court decision.</title>
<headline>B.A.T lifted by Maryland court decision.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in B.A.T Industries Plc rose in a declining UK equity market on Thursday, after a U.S. court ruling dealt a blow to attempts by U.S. states to sue tobacco companies for healthcare costs.</p>
<p>B.A.T unit Brown &amp; Williamson said a Maryland judge had dismissed nine of 13 counts by the state to recover Medicaid expenditures from it, ruling that it does not have a right to recover Medicaid payments made on behalf of individual smokers.</p>
<p>However, the court also said the state was authorised to proceed with its claims that the companies had violated Maryland's Consumer Protection Act and Antitrust Act.</p>
<p>B.A.T shares, often swung around by U.S. legal developments, were up 5-1/2p at 564 by 0746 GMT.</p>
